IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `dda-core`

-- Dust Diseases Act 2005 (SA) -- THE CLAIMANT'S SEAT: the plaintiff in a dust disease action. Usually that is the
-- injured person (who has or had asbestosis, mesothelioma or another asbestos disease); after a death it is the person
-- suing for it (the estate, or the dependants). Every question is asked as that person would ask it, from facts that
-- person can state; what the Act leaves to the court's judgment is asked as a fact ("if the court is satisfied ...").
-- The rules are in dda-core.l4; this module restates none of them.
--
-- Based on content from the South Australian Legislation website at 6 November 2026 (Act version of 1 January 2021;
-- Regulations version of 17 June 2021). CC BY 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `The claimant's questions`

§§ `Is it a dust disease action, and does the Act apply (s 3, Sch 1 cl 4)`

@export Is my claim a "dust disease action" under the Dust Diseases Act 2005 (SA), so that its faster procedures, presumptions and damages rules apply (s 3)?
GIVEN `the disease` IS A `Disease` @desc The disease you have or had (or that the person whose death you claim for had): asbestosis; asbestos induced carcinoma (a cancer caused by asbestos); asbestos related pleural disease; mesothelioma; or another disease or pathological condition (for example silicosis or another dust disease)
      `it resulted from exposure to asbestos dust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For another disease or condition: whether it resulted from exposure to asbestos dust (asbestosis, asbestos induced carcinoma, asbestos related pleural disease and mesothelioma count whatever you answer)
      `my action is a civil action claiming damages for the disease or a death from it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your claim is a civil action (a court claim, not a workers compensation or other statutory claim) for damages for the disease, or for the death of a person from it
      `I say another person's breach of duty caused the disease wholly or partly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you say the disease was wholly or partly caused by another person's (for example an employer's or a manufacturer's) breach of a duty owed to the person who had the disease
GIVETH A `Dust disease action answer`
`Is my claim a dust disease action` MEANS
    `is it a dust disease action (s 3)` `the disease` `it resulted from exposure to asbestos dust` `my action is a civil action claiming damages for the disease or a death from it` `I say another person's breach of duty caused the disease wholly or partly`

@export Does the Dust Diseases Act 2005 (SA) apply to my action, given when it was started (Schedule 1 clause 4: the Act commenced on 8 February 2006)?
GIVEN `the day I commenced the action` IS A DATE @desc The day you commenced (started) the court action
      `the trial has commenced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the trial of the action has begun
      `the day the trial commenced` IS A DATE @desc The day the trial began (any date if it has not)
GIVETH A `Application answer`
`Does the Act apply to my action` MEANS
    `does the Act apply to the action (Sch 1 cl 4)` `the day I commenced the action` `the trial has commenced` `the day the trial commenced`

§§ `Where the action is heard, and how quickly (ss 4A, 5)`

@export Where can I bring my dust disease action (Dust Diseases Act 2005 (SA) s 4A(1), (2))?
GIVEN `the disease` IS A `Disease` @desc The disease you have or had (or that the person whose death you claim for had): asbestosis; asbestos induced carcinoma; asbestos related pleural disease; mesothelioma; or another disease or pathological condition
      `it resulted from exposure to asbestos dust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For another disease or condition: whether it resulted from exposure to asbestos dust
      `my action is a civil action claiming damages for the disease or a death from it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your claim is a civil action for damages for the disease, or for the death of a person from it
      `I say another person's breach of duty caused the disease wholly or partly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you say another person's breach of duty caused the disease wholly or partly
GIVETH A `Forum answer`
`Where can I bring my dust disease action` MEANS
    `where can the action be heard (s 4A(1), (2))` (`is a dust disease action (s 3)` `the disease` `it resulted from exposure to asbestos dust` `my action is a civil action claiming damages for the disease or a death from it` `I say another person's breach of duty caused the disease wholly or partly`)

@export Can I include another claim, or a related matter, in my dust disease proceedings in the South Australian Employment Tribunal (Dust Diseases Act 2005 (SA) s 4A(4), (5))?
GIVEN `my proceedings are in SAET on a dust disease action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your proceedings are in the South Australian Employment Tribunal (SAET) on a dust disease action (or on a claim for contribution between those liable for one)
      `the other claim arises from the same cause of action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other claim arises from the same cause of action (the same wrong) as the dust disease claim, even though it is not about a dust disease
      `the matter is ancillary or related` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the matter is ancillary or related to what the proceedings are about
GIVETH A `Joinder answer`
`Can I include another claim in my SAET proceedings` MEANS
    `can the other claim be included (s 4A(4), (5))` `my proceedings are in SAET on a dust disease action` `the other claim arises from the same cause of action` `the matter is ancillary or related`

@export Will my dust disease action be given priority over less urgent cases (Dust Diseases Act 2005 (SA) s 5)?
GIVEN `the disease` IS A `Disease` @desc The disease you have or had (or that the person whose death you claim for had): asbestosis; asbestos induced carcinoma; asbestos related pleural disease; mesothelioma; or another disease or pathological condition
      `it resulted from exposure to asbestos dust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For another disease or condition: whether it resulted from exposure to asbestos dust
      `my action is a civil action claiming damages for the disease or a death from it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your claim is a civil action for damages for the disease, or for the death of a person from it
      `I say another person's breach of duty caused the disease wholly or partly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you say another person's breach of duty caused the disease wholly or partly
GIVETH A `Priority answer`
`Will my action be given priority` MEANS
    `will the action have priority (s 5)` (`is a dust disease action (s 3)` `the disease` `it resulted from exposure to asbestos dust` `my action is a civil action claiming damages for the disease or a death from it` `I say another person's breach of duty caused the disease wholly or partly`)

§§ `Costs (s 7)`

@export On what basis will costs be allowed or awarded in my dust disease action (Dust Diseases Act 2005 (SA) s 7)?
GIVEN `the disease` IS A `Disease` @desc The disease you have or had (or that the person whose death you claim for had): asbestosis; asbestos induced carcinoma; asbestos related pleural disease; mesothelioma; or another disease or pathological condition
      `it resulted from exposure to asbestos dust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For another disease or condition: whether it resulted from exposure to asbestos dust
      `my action is a civil action claiming damages for the disease or a death from it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your claim is a civil action for damages for the disease, or for the death of a person from it
      `I say another person's breach of duty caused the disease wholly or partly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you say another person's breach of duty caused the disease wholly or partly
      `the court` IS A `Court` @desc Where your action is: the District Court; SAET (the South Australian Employment Tribunal); or another court
      `my action is within the Magistrates Court's jurisdictional limits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your action falls within the Magistrates Court's jurisdictional limits (the size of claim that court can hear)
      `the court considers the Magistrates Court basis appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court considers it appropriate to allow costs on the Magistrates Court basis
GIVETH A `Costs answer`
`On what basis will costs be allowed in my action` MEANS
    `on what basis are costs allowed (s 7)` (`is a dust disease action (s 3)` `the disease` `it resulted from exposure to asbestos dust` `my action is a civil action claiming damages for the disease or a death from it` `I say another person's breach of duty caused the disease wholly or partly`) `the court` `my action is within the Magistrates Court's jurisdictional limits` `the court considers the Magistrates Court basis appropriate`

§§ `Proving the claim (s 8)`

@export Will it be presumed that my exposure to asbestos dust caused or contributed to my dust disease (Dust Diseases Act 2005 (SA) s 8(1))?
GIVEN `the disease` IS A `Disease` @desc The disease you have or had (or that the person whose death you claim for had): asbestosis; asbestos induced carcinoma; asbestos related pleural disease; mesothelioma; or another disease or pathological condition
      `it resulted from exposure to asbestos dust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For another disease or condition: whether it resulted from exposure to asbestos dust
      `my action is a civil action claiming damages for the disease or a death from it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your claim is a civil action for damages for the disease, or for the death of a person from it
      `I say another person's breach of duty caused the disease wholly or partly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you say another person's breach of duty caused the disease wholly or partly
      `it is established that I suffer or suffered from a dust disease` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is established in the action (proved or admitted) that you suffer or suffered from the dust disease
      `it is established that I was exposed in circumstances that might have caused or contributed to it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is established that you were exposed to asbestos dust in circumstances in which that exposure might have caused or contributed to the disease
      `the defendant proves the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the defendant proves that the exposure did not cause or contribute to the disease
GIVETH A `Causation presumption answer`
`Will it be presumed that my exposure caused my disease` MEANS
    `is causation presumed (s 8(1))` (`is a dust disease action (s 3)` `the disease` `it resulted from exposure to asbestos dust` `my action is a civil action claiming damages for the disease or a death from it` `I say another person's breach of duty caused the disease wholly or partly`) `it is established that I suffer or suffered from a dust disease` `it is established that I was exposed in circumstances that might have caused or contributed to it` `the defendant proves the contrary`

@export Is the defendant presumed to have known that exposure to asbestos dust could cause a dust disease, because of the kind of business it carried on (Dust Diseases Act 2005 (SA) s 8(2); Dust Diseases Regulations 2021 reg 4 and Schedule 1)?
GIVEN `the process` IS A `Process` @desc What the defendant was doing when the exposure could have happened: mining or milling of asbestos (or associated packing or transport); manufacture of asbestos products; packing or transport of asbestos products by their manufacturer; sale or supply of asbestos products by their manufacturer; use of asbestos products by their manufacturer; design of an object or thing containing asbestos; sale or other supply of asbestos products by someone other than the manufacturer; installation of asbestos products; use of asbestos products by someone other than the manufacturer; another industrial or commercial process involving asbestos; or a process not involving asbestos
      `the number of persons the defendant employed at the time` IS A NUMBER @desc How many persons the defendant's business employed at the time of that process
      `the only involvement of asbestos was its presence in the structure of the premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For another process involving asbestos: whether the only asbestos involved was asbestos in the building or structure where the work happened
      `the day the process was carried on` IS A DATE @desc The day (or the first day) the defendant carried on the process at the time in question, for example the day of your exposure
      `it could have resulted in my exposure to asbestos dust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the process could have exposed another person (such as you) to asbestos dust
      `the defendant proves it did not know` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the defendant proves that it did not know at the time that exposure to asbestos dust could cause a dust disease
GIVETH A `Knowledge presumption answer`
`Is the defendant presumed to have known of the danger` MEANS
    `is knowledge presumed (s 8(2))` `the process` `the number of persons the defendant employed at the time` `the only involvement of asbestos was its presence in the structure of the premises` `the day the process was carried on` `it could have resulted in my exposure to asbestos dust` `the defendant proves it did not know`

@export Can evidence admitted in an earlier dust disease action against the same defendant be used in my action (Dust Diseases Act 2005 (SA) s 8(3)(a))?
GIVEN `the disease` IS A `Disease` @desc The disease you have or had (or that the person whose death you claim for had): asbestosis; asbestos induced carcinoma; asbestos related pleural disease; mesothelioma; or another disease or pathological condition
      `it resulted from exposure to asbestos dust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For another disease or condition: whether it resulted from exposure to asbestos dust
      `my action is a civil action claiming damages for the disease or a death from it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your claim is a civil action for damages for the disease, or for the death of a person from it
      `I say another person's breach of duty caused the disease wholly or partly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you say another person's breach of duty caused the disease wholly or partly
      `the court` IS A `Court` @desc Where your action is: the District Court; SAET (the South Australian Employment Tribunal); or another court
      `the evidence was admitted in an earlier dust disease action against the same defendant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the evidence was admitted in an earlier dust disease action against the same defendant (in South Australia, or in a court or tribunal of the Commonwealth or another State or Territory)
GIVETH A `Evidence answer`
`Can earlier evidence against the same defendant be used in my action` MEANS
    `can earlier evidence be admitted (s 8(3)(a))` (`is a dust disease action (s 3)` `the disease` `it resulted from exposure to asbestos dust` `my action is a civil action claiming damages for the disease or a death from it` `I say another person's breach of duty caused the disease wholly or partly`) `the court` `the evidence was admitted in an earlier dust disease action against the same defendant`

@export Do I have to prove a matter that is not seriously in dispute (Dust Diseases Act 2005 (SA) s 8(3)(b))?
GIVEN `the disease` IS A `Disease` @desc The disease you have or had (or that the person whose death you claim for had): asbestosis; asbestos induced carcinoma; asbestos related pleural disease; mesothelioma; or another disease or pathological condition
      `it resulted from exposure to asbestos dust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For another disease or condition: whether it resulted from exposure to asbestos dust
      `my action is a civil action claiming damages for the disease or a death from it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your claim is a civil action for damages for the disease, or for the death of a person from it
      `I say another person's breach of duty caused the disease wholly or partly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you say another person's breach of duty caused the disease wholly or partly
      `the court` IS A `Court` @desc Where your action is: the District Court; SAET (the South Australian Employment Tribunal); or another court
      `the matter appears to the court not to be seriously in dispute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the matter appears to the court to be not seriously in dispute
GIVETH A `Proof answer`
`Must I prove a matter not seriously in dispute` MEANS
    `must the matter be proved (s 8(3)(b))` (`is a dust disease action (s 3)` `the disease` `it resulted from exposure to asbestos dust` `my action is a civil action claiming damages for the disease or a death from it` `I say another person's breach of duty caused the disease wholly or partly`) `the court` `the matter appears to the court not to be seriously in dispute`

@export If I decline the court's invitation to admit minor facts, can I be ordered to pay the costs of proving them (Dust Diseases Act 2005 (SA) s 8(3)(c))?
GIVEN `the disease` IS A `Disease` @desc The disease you have or had (or that the person whose death you claim for had): asbestosis; asbestos induced carcinoma; asbestos related pleural disease; mesothelioma; or another disease or pathological condition
      `it resulted from exposure to asbestos dust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For another disease or condition: whether it resulted from exposure to asbestos dust
      `my action is a civil action claiming damages for the disease or a death from it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your claim is a civil action for damages for the disease, or for the death of a person from it
      `I say another person's breach of duty caused the disease wholly or partly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you say another person's breach of duty caused the disease wholly or partly
      `the court` IS A `Court` @desc Where your action is: the District Court; SAET (the South Australian Employment Tribunal); or another court
      `the facts are formal or peripheral to the major issues` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the facts are of a formal nature, or peripheral to the major issues in dispute
      `the court invited me to admit them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court invited you to admit those facts
      `I declined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you declined to admit them
GIVETH A `Admission costs answer`
`Can I be made to pay the costs of proving facts I would not admit` MEANS
    `can the costs of proving the facts be awarded against the party (s 8(3)(c))` (`is a dust disease action (s 3)` `the disease` `it resulted from exposure to asbestos dust` `my action is a civil action claiming damages for the disease or a death from it` `I say another person's breach of duty caused the disease wholly or partly`) `the court` `the facts are formal or peripheral to the major issues` `the court invited me to admit them` `I declined`

@export Can a finding of fact made in an earlier dust disease case be applied in my action (Dust Diseases Act 2005 (SA) s 8(4))?
GIVEN `the disease` IS A `Disease` @desc The disease you have or had (or that the person whose death you claim for had): asbestosis; asbestos induced carcinoma; asbestos related pleural disease; mesothelioma; or another disease or pathological condition
      `it resulted from exposure to asbestos dust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For another disease or condition: whether it resulted from exposure to asbestos dust
      `my action is a civil action claiming damages for the disease or a death from it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your claim is a civil action for damages for the disease, or for the death of a person from it
      `I say another person's breach of duty caused the disease wholly or partly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you say another person's breach of duty caused the disease wholly or partly
      `the court` IS A `Court` @desc Where your action is: the District Court; SAET (the South Australian Employment Tribunal); or another court
      `the finding was made in an earlier dust disease action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the finding of fact was made in an earlier dust disease action
      `the body that made it` IS AN `Earlier body` @desc Who made the finding: a court of South Australia; a court or tribunal of the Commonwealth or another State or Territory; a South Australian tribunal that is not a court; or a court or tribunal outside Australia
      `the court considers it relevant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court hearing your action considers the finding relevant to it
      `the party adversely affected satisfies the court it is inappropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the party the finding would harm satisfies the court that a corresponding finding is inappropriate to the circumstances of your case
GIVETH A `Earlier finding answer`
`Can an earlier finding be applied in my action` MEANS
    `can the earlier finding be applied (s 8(4))` (`is a dust disease action (s 3)` `the disease` `it resulted from exposure to asbestos dust` `my action is a civil action claiming damages for the disease or a death from it` `I say another person's breach of duty caused the disease wholly or partly`) `the court` `the finding was made in an earlier dust disease action` `the body that made it` `the court considers it relevant` `the party adversely affected satisfies the court it is inappropriate`

§§ `Damages (s 9)`

@export Can I be awarded damages now, and further damages later if I develop another dust disease (Dust Diseases Act 2005 (SA) s 9(1))?
GIVEN `the disease` IS A `Disease` @desc The disease you have or had (or that the person whose death you claim for had): asbestosis; asbestos induced carcinoma; asbestos related pleural disease; mesothelioma; or another disease or pathological condition
      `it resulted from exposure to asbestos dust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For another disease or condition: whether it resulted from exposure to asbestos dust
      `my action is a civil action claiming damages for the disease or a death from it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your claim is a civil action for damages for the disease, or for the death of a person from it
      `I say another person's breach of duty caused the disease wholly or partly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you say another person's breach of duty caused the disease wholly or partly
      `it is proved or admitted that I may develop another dust disease from the same breach` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is proved or admitted in the action that you may, at some time in the future, develop another dust disease wholly or partly as a result of the same breach of duty
GIVETH A `Further damages answer`
`Can I get damages now and more later if I develop another dust disease` MEANS
    `can damages be awarded now and later (s 9(1))` (`is a dust disease action (s 3)` `the disease` `it resulted from exposure to asbestos dust` `my action is a civil action claiming damages for the disease or a death from it` `I say another person's breach of duty caused the disease wholly or partly`) `it is proved or admitted that I may develop another dust disease from the same breach`

@export Should I be awarded exemplary (punitive) damages against this defendant (Dust Diseases Act 2005 (SA) s 9(2) and s 8(2); Dust Diseases Regulations 2021 regs 4 and 5, Schedules 1 and 2)?
GIVEN `the disease` IS A `Disease` @desc The disease you have or had (or that the person whose death you claim for had): asbestosis; asbestos induced carcinoma; asbestos related pleural disease; mesothelioma; or another disease or pathological condition
      `it resulted from exposure to asbestos dust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For another disease or condition: whether it resulted from exposure to asbestos dust
      `my action is a civil action claiming damages for the disease or a death from it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your claim is a civil action for damages for the disease, or for the death of a person from it
      `I say another person's breach of duty caused the disease wholly or partly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you say another person's breach of duty caused the disease wholly or partly
      `the court is satisfied the defendant knew I was at risk of exposure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court is satisfied that the defendant knew you were at risk of exposure to asbestos dust
      `the process` IS A `Process` @desc What the defendant was doing that exposed you: mining or milling of asbestos (or associated packing or transport); manufacture of asbestos products; packing or transport of asbestos products by their manufacturer; sale or supply of asbestos products by their manufacturer; use of asbestos products by their manufacturer; design of an object or thing containing asbestos; sale or other supply of asbestos products by someone other than the manufacturer; installation of asbestos products; use of asbestos products by someone other than the manufacturer; another industrial or commercial process involving asbestos; or a process not involving asbestos
      `the number of persons the defendant employed at the time` IS A NUMBER @desc How many persons the defendant's business employed at the time of that process
      `the only involvement of asbestos was its presence in the structure of the premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For another process involving asbestos: whether the only asbestos involved was asbestos in the building or structure where the work happened
      `the day of my exposure` IS A DATE @desc The day (or the first day) of your exposure to asbestos dust from that process
      `the process resulted in my exposure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that process resulted in your exposure to asbestos dust
      `the court is satisfied on the evidence that the defendant knew of the danger` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court is satisfied on the evidence (apart from any presumption) that the defendant knew, at the time of your exposure, that exposure to asbestos dust could cause a dust disease
      `the defendant proves it did not know` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the defendant proves that it did not know at the time that exposure to asbestos dust could cause a dust disease
GIVETH A `Exemplary damages answer`
`Should I be awarded exemplary damages against this defendant` MEANS
    `should exemplary damages be awarded (s 9(2))` (`is a dust disease action (s 3)` `the disease` `it resulted from exposure to asbestos dust` `my action is a civil action claiming damages for the disease or a death from it` `I say another person's breach of duty caused the disease wholly or partly`) `the court is satisfied the defendant knew I was at risk of exposure` `the process` `the number of persons the defendant employed at the time` `the only involvement of asbestos was its presence in the structure of the premises` `the day of my exposure` `the process resulted in my exposure` `the court is satisfied on the evidence that the defendant knew of the danger` `the defendant proves it did not know`

@export Will I be compensated for losing (or losing some of) my capacity to do domestic work for other people, such as caring for my family (Dust Diseases Act 2005 (SA) s 9(3))?
GIVEN `the disease` IS A `Disease` @desc The disease you have or had (or that the person whose death you claim for had): asbestosis; asbestos induced carcinoma; asbestos related pleural disease; mesothelioma; or another disease or pathological condition
      `it resulted from exposure to asbestos dust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For another disease or condition: whether it resulted from exposure to asbestos dust
      `my action is a civil action claiming damages for the disease or a death from it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your claim is a civil action for damages for the disease, or for the death of a person from it
      `I say another person's breach of duty caused the disease wholly or partly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you say another person's breach of duty caused the disease wholly or partly
      `my capacity to perform domestic services for another person is lost or impaired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the disease has taken away or reduced your capacity to perform domestic services (housework, care) for another person
GIVETH A `Domestic services answer`
`Will I be compensated for my lost capacity to do domestic work for others` MEANS
    `is the lost capacity for domestic services compensated (s 9(3))` (`is a dust disease action (s 3)` `the disease` `it resulted from exposure to asbestos dust` `my action is a civil action claiming damages for the disease or a death from it` `I say another person's breach of duty caused the disease wholly or partly`) `my capacity to perform domestic services for another person is lost or impaired`

§§ `Several defendants, and suing the insurer (ss 10, 11)`
-- Situation: there is more than one defendant or insurer, or the person responsible has died, been dissolved, become
-- insolvent or cannot be found.

@export Will my claim be decided before the defendants' or insurers' disputes about contribution between themselves (Dust Diseases Act 2005 (SA) s 10)?
GIVEN `the disease` IS A `Disease` @desc The disease you have or had (or that the person whose death you claim for had): asbestosis; asbestos induced carcinoma; asbestos related pleural disease; mesothelioma; or another disease or pathological condition
      `it resulted from exposure to asbestos dust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For another disease or condition: whether it resulted from exposure to asbestos dust
      `my action is a civil action claiming damages for the disease or a death from it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your claim is a civil action for damages for the disease, or for the death of a person from it
      `I say another person's breach of duty caused the disease wholly or partly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you say another person's breach of duty caused the disease wholly or partly
      `several defendants or insurers are involved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there are several defendants or insurers in your action
      `the court considers the delay from dealing with them together inconsequential` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court considers that any delay from deciding your claim and their contribution questions together would be inconsequential
GIVETH A `Order of questions answer`
`Will my claim be decided before contribution between the defendants` MEANS
    `is liability to the plaintiff decided first (s 10)` (`is a dust disease action (s 3)` `the disease` `it resulted from exposure to asbestos dust` `my action is a civil action claiming damages for the disease or a death from it` `I say another person's breach of duty caused the disease wholly or partly`) `several defendants or insurers are involved` `the court considers the delay from dealing with them together inconsequential`

@export Can I sue the defendant's insurer directly (Dust Diseases Act 2005 (SA) s 11(1), (2))?
GIVEN `the disease` IS A `Disease` @desc The disease you have or had (or that the person whose death you claim for had): asbestosis; asbestos induced carcinoma; asbestos related pleural disease; mesothelioma; or another disease or pathological condition
      `it resulted from exposure to asbestos dust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For another disease or condition: whether it resulted from exposure to asbestos dust
      `my action is a civil action claiming damages for the disease or a death from it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your claim is a civil action for damages for the disease, or for the death of a person from it
      `I say another person's breach of duty caused the disease wholly or partly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you say another person's breach of duty caused the disease wholly or partly
      `the defendant's status` IS A `Defendant status` @desc What has happened to the person you would sue: dead; dissolved (a company wound up and deregistered); insolvent; cannot be found; or none of these
      `the insurer insured the defendant against the liability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer insured that person against the kind of liability your action is about
GIVETH A `Direct action answer`
`Can I sue the defendant's insurer directly` MEANS
    `can the insurer be sued directly (s 11(1), (2))` (`is a dust disease action (s 3)` `the disease` `it resulted from exposure to asbestos dust` `my action is a civil action claiming damages for the disease or a death from it` `I say another person's breach of duty caused the disease wholly or partly`) `the defendant's status` `the insurer insured the defendant against the liability`

@export If I sue the insurer directly, what is the most I can recover from it (Dust Diseases Act 2005 (SA) s 11(2), (3))?
GIVEN `the damages the defendant would have been liable for` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount (in dollars) the defendant would have been liable to pay you had you sued the defendant
      `the amount the insurer would have indemnified` IS A NUMBER @desc The most (in dollars) the insurer would have been liable to pay the defendant under its insurance for that liability
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much can I recover from the insurer` MEANS
    `the insurer's liability (s 11(2), (3))` `the damages the defendant would have been liable for` `the amount the insurer would have indemnified`

§§ `Appeals (s 11A)`
-- Situation: SAET has made a decision in your dust disease action that you want to appeal.

@export Where does an appeal against a decision of the South Australian Employment Tribunal in my dust disease action go (Dust Diseases Act 2005 (SA) s 11A)?
GIVEN `it is a decision of SAET in or about my dust disease action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the decision is one of the South Australian Employment Tribunal (SAET) in or about your dust disease action (including an ancillary or related matter in the proceedings)
      `the decision` IS A `Decision kind` @desc The kind of decision: an interlocutory order (a decision along the way, before the final judgment); or any other decision (such as the final judgment)
GIVETH A `Appeal answer`
`Where does my appeal go` MEANS
    `where does the appeal lie (s 11A)` `it is a decision of SAET in or about my dust disease action` `the decision`
